<title>USA: U.S. Aug import prices fell 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug import prices fell 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Department report of U.S. import and export price changes by percent (unadjusted).</p>
<p>    -			   Aug  July-Rev from   Aug96/95</p>
<p> ALL IMPORTS		 -0.2   -0.1  -0.2     -0.5</p>
<p> -Petroleum		  -0.2    2.3   1.5     17.7</p>
<p> -Nonpetroleum	     -0.2   -0.4  -0.4     -2.2</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	-0.8   -1.3  -1.2     -4.5</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies    -0.1    0.1  UNCH	3.1</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	    -0.4   -0.2  -0.3     -4.0</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts   UNCH    0.2   0.2	0.3</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos -0.1   -0.1  -0.2     -0.4</p>
<p>Percent changes, not seasonally adjusted --</p>
<p> ALL EXPORTS		 -0.1   -0.5  -0.5	0.5</p>
<p> -Agricultural	     -0.2   -1.9  -2.0     15.1</p>
<p> -Non-Agricultural	 -0.1   -0.2  -0.3     -1.4</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	-0.5   -1.4  -1.4     17.1</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies    -0.3   -0.5  -0.6     -5.8</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	    UNCH   -0.3  -0.3	0.5</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts    0.2   -0.1  UNCH	1.5</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos  0.1   UNCH  UNCH	1.1</p>
<p>The department reported August price indexes (1990 base year equals 100) of 106.2 for imports, and 109.7 for exports.</p>
</text>
